an(host, port)\", () -> Ra.cp(Scanner.scan(\"relay\", 22).contains(\"22\"), \"scan(host, port)\", Scanner.scan(\"relay\", 22)));\n        Ra.tryCp(\"sum varargs\", () -> Ra.eq(\"sum varargs\", Scanner.sum(1, 2, 3, 4), 10));\n        Ra.tryCp(\"sum of nothing\", () -> Ra.eq(\"sum of nothing\", Scanner.sum(), 0));\n    }\n}\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n","jv5":"// @cp shift 3 | wraps z to c | keeps case and punctuation | round trip\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Ra.tryCp(\"shift 3\", () -> Ra.eq(\"shift 3\", Cipher.caesar(\"abc\", 3), \"def\"));\n        Ra.tryCp(\"wraps z to c\", () -> Ra.eq(\"wraps z to c\", Cipher.caesar(\"xyz\", 3), \"abc\"));\n        Ra.tryCp(\"keeps case and punctuation\", () -> Ra.eq(\"keeps case and punctuation\", Cipher.caesar(\"Hello, World!\", 1), \"Ifmmp, Xpsme!\"));\n        Ra.tryCp(\"round trip\", () -> Ra.eq(\"round trip\", Cipher.caesar(Cipher.caesar(\"Matrix\", 7), 19), \"Matrix\"));\n    }\n}\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n","jv6":"// @cp record accessors | records compare by value | compact constructor rejects bad input | Session field is private final\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Ra.tryCp(\"record accessors\", () -> { Node n = new Node(\"north\", 40); Ra.cp(n.name().equals(\"north\") && n.strength() == 40, \"record accessors\", n.toString()); });\n        Ra.tryCp(\"records compare by value\", () -> Ra.eq(\"records compare by value\", new Node(\"a\", 1), new Node(\"a\", 1)));\n        boolean threw = false;\n        try { new Node(null, -1); } catch (RuntimeException e) { threw = true; }\n        try { if (!threw) new Node(\"\", -5); } catch (RuntimeException e) { threw = true; }\n        Ra.cp(threw, \"compact constructor rejects bad input\", \"new Node(null, -1) and new Node(\\\"\\\", -5) were both accepted\");\n        boolean pf = false;\n        for (var f : Session.class.getDeclaredFields()) { int m = f.getModifiers(); if (java.lang.reflect.Modifier.isPrivate(m) && java.lang.reflect.Modifier.isFinal(m)) pf = true; }\n        Ra.cp(pf, \"Session field is private final\", \"\");\n    }\n}\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n","jv7":"// @cp parsePort ok | garbage throws BadPortException | BadPortException is checked\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Ra.tryCp(\"parsePort ok\", () -> Ra.eq(\"parsePort ok\", Ports.parsePort(\"443\"), 443));\n        try { Ports.parsePort(\"http\"); Ra.cp(false, \"garbage throws BadPortException\", \"no exception\"); }\n        catch (BadPortException e) { Ra.cp(true, \"garbage throws BadPortException\", \"\"); }\n        catch (Throwable t) { Ra.cp(false, \"garbage throws BadPortException\", \"threw \" + t); }\n        Ra.cp(Exception.class.isAssignableFrom(BadPortException.class) && !RuntimeException.class.isAssignableFrom(BadPortException.class), \"BadPortException is checked\", \"\");\n    }\n}\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n","jv8":"// @cp Keyword detects substrings | Keyword is a Rule and a Detector | Detector has a default method\nimport java.util.*;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Ra.tryCp(\"Keyword detects substrings\", () -> { Keyword k = new Keyword(\"jndi\"); Ra.cp(k.detect(\"${jndi:x}\") && !k.detect(\"hello\"), \"Keyword detects substrings\", \"\"); });\n        Ra.cp(Rule.class.isAssignableFrom(Keyword.class) && Detector.class.isAssignableFrom(Rule.class) && java.lang.reflect.Modifier.isAbstract(Rule.class.getModifiers()), \"Keyword is a Rule and a Detector\", \"\");\n        boolean def = false;\n        for (var m : Detector.class.getDeclaredMethods()) if (m.isDefault()) def = true;\n        Ra.cp(def, \"Detector has a default method\", \"\");\n    }\n}\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n","jv9":"// @cp strongest of ints | strongest of strings | Box holds a value\nimport java.util.*;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Ra.tryCp(\"strongest of ints\", () -> Ra.eq(\"strongest of ints\", __CLASS_OF:strongest__.strongest(List.of(3, 9, 2)), 9));\n        Ra.tryCp(\"strongest of strings\", () -> Ra.eq(\"strongest of strings\", __CLASS_OF:strongest__.strongest(List.of(\"alpha\", \"omega\", \"beta\")), \"omega\"));\n        Ra.tryCp(\"Box holds a value\", () -> Ra.cp(Box.class.getTypeParameters().length == 1, \"Box holds a value\", \"Box should declare one type parameter\"));\n    }\n}\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n","kt1":"// @cp intro(\"neo\", 3) | intro(\"trinity\", 12) | main runs\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    raTry(\"intro(\\\"neo\\\", 3)\") { raEq(\"intro(\\\"neo\\\", 3)\", intro(\"neo\", 3), \"Agent neo // level 3\") }\n    raTry(\"intro(\\\"trinity\\\", 12)\") { raEq(\"intro(\\\"trinity\\\", 12)\", intro(\"trinity\", 12), \"Agent trinity // level 12\") }\n    raTry(\"main runs\") { raUserMain(); raCp(true, \"main runs\") }\n}\n","kt10":"// @cp ping returns true for a host | sweep counts reachable hosts | sweep runs concurrently\n// @ci-only Needs kotlinx.coroutines, which Judge0's Kotlin image doesn't include. Runs in GitHub Actions with the real library.\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.*\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() = runBlocking {\n    raTry(\"ping returns true for a host\") { raCp(runBlocking { ping(\"north\") }, \"ping returns true for a host\") }\n    raTry(\"sweep counts reachable hosts\") { raEq(\"sweep counts reachable hosts\", runBlocking { sweep(listOf(\"a\", \"b\", \"c\")) } >= 0, true) }\n    raTry(\"sweep runs concurrently\") {\n        val t0 = System.nanoTime()\n        runBlocking { sweep(List(50) { \"h$it\" }) }\n        val ms = (System.nanoTime() - t0) / 1_000_000\n        val one = run { val s = System.nanoTime(); runBlocking { ping(\"x\") }; (System.nanoTime() - s) / 1_000_000 }\n        raCp(ms < one * 10 + 500, \"sweep runs concurrently\", \"50 hosts took ${ms}ms, one ping takes ${one}ms\")\n    }\n}\n","kt11":"// @cp Your @Test functions pass | At least two @Test functions\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    val obj = __TEST_CLASS__()\n    val tests = obj.javaClass.declaredMethods.filter { it.isAnnotationPresent(Test::class.java) }\n    var failed = 0\n    for (m in tests) {\n        try { m.isAccessible = true; m.invoke(obj) } catch (e: java.lang.reflect.InvocationTargetException) { failed++; println(\"test ${m.name} failed: ${e.targetException.message}\") }\n    }\n    raCp(failed == 0 && tests.isNotEmpty(), \"Your @Test functions pass\", \"$failed of ${tests.size} failed\")\n    raCp(tests.size >= 2, \"At least two @Test functions\", \"found ${tests.size}\")\n}\n","kt12":"// @cp ViewModel exposes a StateFlow | UI state is a sealed type | Screen composes a Button | Clicking the Button updates the StateFlow | Screen composes a LazyColumn\n// @ci-only Needs kotlinx.coroutines plus Compose/AndroidX API stubs (tools/ci/stubs/kotlin). Runs in GitHub Actions.\nimport ra.compose.RaCompose\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.flow.StateFlow\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    val vm = __VM_CLASS__()\n    val getter = vm.javaClass.methods.firstOrNull { StateFlow::class.java.isAssignableFrom(it.returnType) && it.parameterCount == 0 }\n    raCp(getter != null, \"ViewModel exposes a StateFlow\", \"no public StateFlow property on __VM_CLASS__\")\n    if (getter == null) return\n    val flow = getter.invoke(vm) as StateFlow<*>\n    val first = flow.value\n    val sealedTypes = __SEALED__.mapNotNull { runCatching { Class.forName(it) }.getOrNull() }\n    raCp(first != null && sealedTypes.any { it.isInstance(first) }, \"UI state is a sealed type\", \"state value ${first} isn't an instance of a sealed class/interface you declared\")\n    val screen = Class.forName(\"MainKt\").methods.first { it.name == \"__SCREEN__\" }\n    fun render() { RaCompose.reset(); if (screen.parameterCount == 0) screen.invoke(null) else screen.invoke(null, vm) }\n    render()\n    val firstCalls = RaCompose.calls.toList()\n    raCp(\"Button\" in firstCalls, \"Screen composes a Button\", \"composed: $firstCalls\")\n    val click = RaCompose.onClicks.firstOrNull()\n    val seen = mutableSetOf<Any?>(first)\n    if (click != null) {\n        click()\n        val end = System.currentTimeMillis() + 3000\n        while (System.currentTimeMillis() < end && seen.size < 2) { seen.add(flow.value); Thread.sleep(5) }\n        Thread.sleep(300); seen.add(flow.value)\n    }\n    raCp(seen.size >= 2, \"Clicking the Button updates the StateFlow\", \"state stayed $first for 3s after onClick\")\n    render()\n    raCp(\"LazyColumn\" in firstCalls || \"LazyColumn\" in RaCompose.calls, \"Screen composes a LazyColumn\", \"composed: ${RaCompose.calls}\")\n}\n","kt2":"// @cp score 95 | score 90 | score 60 | score 59 | score 30 | score 0\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    for ((s, w) in listOf(95 to \"CRITICAL\", 90 to \"CRITICAL\", 60 to \"HIGH\", 59 to \"MEDIUM\", 30 to \"MEDIUM\", 0 to \"LOW\"))\n        raTry(\"score $s\") { raEq(\"score $s\", threatLevel(s), w) }\n}\n","kt3":"// @cp tally counts | tally empty\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    raTry(\"tally counts\") { raEq(\"tally counts\", tally(listOf(\"a\", \"b\", \"a\")), mapOf(\"a\" to 2, \"b\" to 1)) }\n    raTry(\"tally empty\") { raEq(\"tally empty\", tally(emptyList()), emptyMap<String, Int>()) }\n}\n","kt4":"// @cp scan uses the default port | scan with a named port | isPrivateIp true for 10.x and 192.168.x | isPrivateIp false for public IPs\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    raTry(\"scan uses the default port\") { raCp(scan(\"relay\").contains(\"443\"), \"scan uses the default port\", scan(\"relay\")) }\n    raTry(\"scan with a named port\") { raCp(scan(\"relay\", port = 22).contains(\"22\"), \"scan with a named port\", scan(\"relay\", port = 22)) }\n    raTry(\"isPrivateIp true for 10.x and 192.168.x\") { raCp(\"10.0.0.4\".isPrivateIp() && \"192.168.1.7\".isPrivateIp(), \"isPrivateIp true for 10.x and 192.168.x\") }\n    raTry(\"isPrivateIp false for public IPs\") { raCp(!\"8.8.8.8\".isPrivateIp(), \"isPrivateIp false for public IPs\") }\n}\n","kt5":"// @cp lookup finds a name | lookup falls back to unknown | parseKv\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    raTry(\"lookup finds a name\") { raEq(\"lookup finds a name\", lookup(\"relay\", mapOf(\"relay\" to \"10.0.0.4\")), \"10.0.0.4\") }\n    raTry(\"lookup falls back to unknown\") { raEq(\"lookup falls back to unknown\", lookup(\"ghost\", mapOf(\"relay\" to \"10.0.0.4\")), \"unknown\") }\n    raTry(\"parseKv\") {\n        val seps = listOf(\"host=relay;port=22\", \"host=relay,port=22\", \"host=relay&port=22\", \"host=relay port=22\")\n        val ok = seps.any { s -> runCatching { parseKv(s) }.getOrNull().let { it?.get(\"host\") == \"relay\" && it[\"port\"] == \"22\" } }\n        raCp(ok, \"parseKv\", \"parseKv(\\\"host=relay;port=22\\\") = ${runCatching { parseKv(\"host=relay;port=22\") }.getOrNull()}\")\n    }\n}\n","kt6":"// @cp Node has a default strength | copy changes one field | data class equality | destructuring\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    raTry(\"Node has a default strength\") { raEq(\"Node has a default strength\", Node(\"north\").strength, 0) }\n    raTry(\"copy changes one field\") { val b = Node(\"north\", 40).copy(strength = 90); raCp(b.name == \"north\" && b.strength == 90, \"copy changes one field\", \"$b\") }\n    raTry(\"data class equality\") { raEq(\"data class equality\", Node(\"a\", 1), Node(\"a\", 1)) }\n    raTry(\"destructuring\") { val (n, s) = Node(\"hill\", 7); raEq(\"destructuring\", \"$n:$s\", \"hill:7\") }\n}\n","kt7":"// @cp parsePort ok | garbage throws | out of range throws | BadPort is an Exception\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    raTry(\"parsePort ok\") { raEq(\"parsePort ok\", parsePort(\"443\"), 443) }\n    raTry(\"garbage throws\") { raCp(runCatching { parsePort(\"http\") }.isFailure, \"garbage throws\") }\n    raTry(\"out of range throws\") { raCp(runCatching { parsePort(\"70000\") }.isFailure && runCatching { parsePort(\"0\") }.isFailure, \"out of range throws\") }\n    raCp(Exception::class.java.isAssignableFrom(BadPort::class.java), \"BadPort is an Exception\")\n}\n","kt8":"// @cp Login and Breach are Events | Logout is a singleton Event | data object prints its name\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    raCp(Event::class.java.isAssignableFrom(Login::class.java) && Event::class.java.isAssignableFrom(Breach::class.java), \"Login and Breach are Events\")\n    raCp((Logout as Any) is Event, \"Logout is a singleton Event\")\n    raEq(\"data object prints its name\", Logout.toString(), \"Logout\")\n}\n","kt9":"// @cp strongest of ints | strongest of strings | strongest of empty | Detector is an interface\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfun main() {\n    raTry(\"strongest of ints\") { raEq(\"strongest of ints\", strongest(listOf(3, 9, 2)), 9) }\n    raTry(\"strongest of strings\") { raEq(\"strongest of strings\", strongest(listOf(\"alpha\", \"omega\", \"beta\")), \"omega\") }\n    raTry(\"strongest of empty\") { raEq(\"strongest of empty\", strongest(emptyList<Int>()), null) }\n    raCp(Detector::class.java.isInterface, \"Detector is an interface\")\n}\n","rs1":"// @cp intro(\"neo\", 3) | intro(\"trinity\", 12) | main runs\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        ra_try(\"intro(\\\"neo\\\", 3)\", || ra_eq(\"intro(\\\"neo\\\", 3)\", intro(\"neo\", 3), \"Agent neo // level 3\".to_string()));\n        ra_try(\"intro(\\\"trinity\\\", 12)\", || ra_eq(\"intro(\\\"trinity\\\", 12)\", intro(\"trinity\", 12), \"Agent trinity // level 12\".to_string()));\n        ra_try(\"main runs\", || { ra_user_main(); ra_cp(true, \"main runs\", \"\"); });\n    }\n}\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs10":"// @cp counts reachable hosts | empty list | 200 threads\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        ra_try(\"counts reachable hosts\", || ra_eq(\"counts reachable hosts\", sweep(vec![\"a\".into(), \"\".into(), \"c\".into()]), 2));\n        ra_try(\"empty list\", || ra_eq(\"empty list\", sweep(vec![]), 0));\n        ra_try(\"200 threads\", || ra_eq(\"200 threads\", sweep((0..200).map(|i| i.to_string()).collect()), 200));\n    }\n}\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs11":"// @cp longest picks the longer | longest with equal lengths | Your #[test] suite\n// @opts --test\n// @args --nocapture --test-threads=1\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        ra_try(\"longest picks the longer\", || ra_eq(\"longest picks the longer\", longest(\"ab\", \"abcd\"), \"abcd\"));\n        ra_try(\"longest with equal lengths\", || { let r = longest(\"ab\", \"cd\"); ra_cp(r == \"ab\" || r == \"cd\", \"longest with equal lengths\", r); });\n    }\n}\n#[test]\nfn ra_checks() { ra_h::run(); }\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs12":"// @cp parse a good line | parse rejects junk | analyze counts | Summary implements Display | Your #[test] suite\n// @opts --test\n// @args --nocapture --test-threads=1\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        ra_try(\"parse a good line\", || { let r = parse(\"1.1.1.1 FAIL\"); ra_cp(matches!(&r, Ok(rec) if rec.ip == \"1.1.1.1\" && matches!(rec.status, Status::Fail)), \"parse a good line\", \"\"); });\n        ra_try(\"parse rejects junk\", || ra_cp(parse(\"junk\").is_err(), \"parse rejects junk\", \"\"));\n        ra_try(\"analyze counts\", || { let s = analyze(&[\"1.1.1.1 FAIL\", \"2.2.2.2 OK\", \"junk\", \"3.3.3.3 FAIL\"]); ra_eq(\"analyze counts\", (s.total, s.fails), (3, 2)); });\n        ra_try(\"Summary implements Display\", || { let s = format!(\"{}\", analyze(&[\"1.1.1.1 FAIL\"])); ra_cp(s.contains('1'), \"Summary implements Display\", &s); });\n    }\n}\n#[test]\nfn ra_checks() { ra_h::run(); }\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs2":"// @cp score 95 | score 90 | score 89 | score 60 | score 59 | score 30 | score 0\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        for (s, w) in [(95u32, \"CRITICAL\"), (90, \"CRITICAL\"), (89, \"HIGH\"), (60, \"HIGH\"), (59, \"MEDIUM\"), (30, \"MEDIUM\"), (0, \"LOW\")] {\n            let l = format!(\"score {}\", s);\n            ra_try(&l.clone(), move || ra_eq(&l, threat_level(s), w));\n        }\n    }\n}\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs3":"// @cp counts repeats | counts singles | empty input\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        let ips: Vec<String> = [\"10.0.0.9\", \"10.0.0.4\", \"10.0.0.9\"].iter().map(|s| s.to_string()).collect();\n        ra_try(\"counts repeats\", || ra_eq(\"counts repeats\", tally(&ips).get(\"10.0.0.9\").copied(), Some(2)));\n        ra_try(\"counts singles\", || ra_eq(\"counts singles\", tally(&ips).get(\"10.0.0.4\").copied(), Some(1)));\n        ra_try(\"empty input\", || ra_eq(\"empty input\", tally(&[]).len(), 0));\n    }\n}\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs4":"// @cp count_words | count_words with extra spaces | redact mutates in place\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        ra_try(\"count_words\", || ra_eq(\"count_words\", count_words(\"the relay is down\"), 4));\n        ra_try(\"count_words with extra spaces\", || ra_eq(\"count_words with extra spaces\", count_words(\"  a   b \\n c \"), 3));\n        ra_try(\"redact mutates in place\", || { let mut m = String::from(\"secret plan\"); redact(&mut m); ra_eq(\"redact mutates in place\", m, \"[REDACTED]\".to_string()); });\n    }\n}\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs5":"// @cp shift 3 | wraps z to c | keeps case and punctuation | round trip\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        ra_try(\"shift 3\", || ra_eq(\"shift 3\", caesar(\"abc\", 3), \"def\".to_string()));\n        ra_try(\"wraps z to c\", || ra_eq(\"wraps z to c\", caesar(\"xyz\", 3), \"abc\".to_string()));\n        ra_try(\"keeps case and punctuation\", || ra_eq(\"keeps case and punctuation\", caesar(\"Hello, World!\", 1), \"Ifmmp, Xpsme!\".to_string()));\n        ra_try(\"round trip\", || ra_eq(\"round trip\", caesar(&caesar(\"Matrix\", 7), 19), \"Matrix\".to_string()));\n    }\n}\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs6":"// @cp new() starts at 0 | boost returns the new strength | Debug is derived | describe covers every variant\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        ra_try(\"new() starts at 0\", || { let n = Node::new(\"north\"); ra_cp(n.name == \"north\" && n.strength == 0, \"new() starts at 0\", &format!(\"{:?}\", n)); });\n        ra_try(\"boost returns the new strength\", || { let mut n = Node::new(\"x\"); n.boost(5); ra_eq(\"boost returns the new strength\", n.boost(3), 8); });\n        ra_try(\"Debug is derived\", || { let d = format!(\"{:?}\", Node::new(\"hill\")); ra_cp(d.contains(\"hill\"), \"Debug is derived\", &d); });\n        ra_try(\"describe covers every variant\", || {\n            let a = describe(&Event::Login(\"neo\".into()));\n            let b = describe(&Event::Breach(9));\n            let c = describe(&Event::Logout);\n            ra_cp(a.contains(\"neo\") && b.contains('9') && !c.is_empty() && a != c, \"describe covers every variant\", &format!(\"{:?} {:?} {:?}\", a, b, c));\n        });\n    }\n}\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs7":"// @cp parse_port ok | empty input is ParseError Empty | garbage is ParseError BadPort | ports() stops at the first error | ports() collects\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        ra_try(\"parse_port ok\", || ra_cp(matches!(parse_port(\"443\"), Ok(443)), \"parse_port ok\", \"\"));\n        ra_try(\"empty input is ParseError Empty\", || ra_cp(matches!(parse_port(\"\"), Err(ParseError::Empty)), \"empty input is ParseError Empty\", \"\"));\n        ra_try(\"garbage is ParseError BadPort\", || ra_cp(matches!(parse_port(\"http\"), Err(ParseError::BadPort(_))), \"garbage is ParseError BadPort\", \"\"));\n        ra_try(\"ports() stops at the first error\", || ra_cp(ports(&[\"22\", \"nope\", \"80\"]).is_err(), \"ports() stops at the first error\", \"\"));\n        ra_try(\"ports() collects\", || ra_cp(matches!(ports(&[\"22\", \"80\"]).as_deref(), Ok([22, 80])), \"ports() collects\", \"\"));\n    }\n}\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs8":"// @cp Keyword detects substrings | count_hits | works through a generic bound\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    struct RaAll;\n    impl Detector for RaAll { fn detect(&self, _l: &str) -> bool { true } }\n    pub fn run() {\n        let k = Keyword(\"jndi\".to_string());\n        ra_try(\"Keyword detects substrings\", || ra_cp(k.detect(\"${jndi:x}\") && !k.detect(\"hello\"), \"Keyword detects substrings\", \"\"));\n        ra_try(\"count_hits\", || ra_eq(\"count_hits\", count_hits(&Keyword(\"jndi\".to_string()), &[\"jndi a\", \"b\", \"c jndi\"]), 2));\n        ra_try(\"works through a generic bound\", || ra_eq(\"works through a generic bound\", count_hits(&RaAll, &[\"a\", \"b\"]), 2));\n    }\n}\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","rs9":"// @cp first word of FAIL lines | ignores other lines | empty input\n//@@USER@@\nmod ra_h {\n    #![allow(unused)]\n    use super::*;\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n    pub fn run() {\n        ra_try(\"first word of FAIL lines\", || ra_eq(\"first word of FAIL lines\", fail_ips(&[\"10.0.0.9 FAIL\", \"10.0.0.4 OK\", \"10.0.0.2 FAIL\"]), vec![\"10.0.0.9\".to_string(), \"10.0.0.2\".to_string()]));\n        ra_try(\"ignores other lines\", || ra_eq(\"ignores other lines\", fail_ips(&[\"FAILOVER ok\", \"x OK\"]).len(), 0));\n        ra_try(\"empty input\", || ra_eq(\"empty input\", fail_ips(&[]).len(), 0));\n    }\n}\nfn main() { ra_h::run(); }\n","sh1":"# @cp creates ops/intel/2026/brief.txt | lists in long format (-l) | lists hidden entries (-a)\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\nra_run\n[ -f ops/intel/2026/brief.txt ]; ra_cp $? \"creates ops/intel/2026/brief.txt\" \"file not found after running your script\"\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -qE '^total [0-9]+'; ra_cp $? \"lists in long format (-l)\" \"no 'total' line in the listing\"\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -qE ' \\.\\.?$'; ra_cp $? \"lists hidden entries (-a)\" \"no . or .. entries in the listing\"\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -q 'brief.txt'\n","sh10":"# @cp prints offline node names | raw output (-r) has no quotes | sends the Bearer token header\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\ncat > bin/curl <<'C'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nauth=0; for a in \"$@\"; do [ \"$a\" = \"Authorization: Bearer s3cret\" ] && auth=1; done\n[ \"$auth\" = 1 ] || { echo \"curl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 401\" >&2; exit 22; }\necho '{\"nodes\":[{\"name\":\"north\",\"online\":true},{\"name\":\"harbor\",\"online\":false},{\"name\":\"relay-7\",\"online\":false}]}'\nC\nchmod +x bin/curl\nif ! command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1; then\ncat > bin/jq <<'JQ'\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# Minimal jq subset (Judge0's Bash image has no jq; CI uses the real one): -r, .a.b, .a[], select(.k == v / != v), pipes.\nimport json, sys, re\nargs = [a for a in sys.argv[1:] if not a.startswith(\"-\")]\nraw = \"-r\" in sys.argv\nflt = args[0] if args else \".\"\ndef path(v, p):\n    out = [v]\n    for tok in re.findall(r\"\\.(\\w+)|(\\[\\])\", p):\n        nxt = []\n        for x in out:\n            if tok[0]: nxt.append(x.get(tok[0]) if isinstance(x, dict) else None)\n            else: nxt.extend(x if isinstance(x, list) else list(x.values()))\n        out = nxt\n    return out\ndef stage(vals, s):\n    s = s.strip()\n    m = re.match(r\"select\\((.+?)\\s*(==|!=)\\s*(.+)\\)$\", s)\n    if m:\n        want = json.loads(m.group(3))\n        return [v for v in vals if (path(v, m.group(1))[0] == want) == (m.group(2) == \"==\")]\n    return [r for v in vals for r in path(v, s)]\nvals = [json.load(sys.stdin)]\nfor s in flt.split(\"|\"): vals = stage(vals, s)\nfor v in vals: print(v if raw and isinstance(v, str) else json.dumps(v))\nJQ\nchmod +x bin/jq; fi\nTOKEN=s3cret; export TOKEN; ra_run\nra_eq \"prints offline node names\" \"$RA_OUT\" \"$(printf 'harbor\\nrelay-7')\"\nprintf '%s' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -q '\"'; [ $? = 1 ]; ra_cp $? \"raw output (-r) has no quotes\" \"$RA_OUT\"\nTOKEN=wrong; ra_run; [ -z \"$RA_OUT\" ]; ra_cp $? \"sends the Bearer token header\" \"with a wrong token you still printed: $RA_OUT\"\n","sh11":"# @cp exports RELAY_ENV=prod | puts HOME/ops/bin first on PATH | cron line runs sweep.sh every 15 minutes | cron line appends stdout and stderr to the log\n# The cron line isn't executed; it's parsed and validated.\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\ncron=$(grep -oE '(^|[\"'\"'\"'(; ])[^ \"'\"'\"'(]+( +[^ ]+){4} +/opt/ops/sweep\\.sh[^\"'\"'\"')]*' user.sh | head -n 1 | sed -E 's/^[\"'\"'\"'(; ]//')\ngrep -v '/opt/ops/sweep\\.sh' user.sh | grep -v 'crontab' > env_only.sh\nenv -i HOME=\"$HOME\" PATH=\"/usr/bin:/bin\" bash -c 'source ./env_only.sh >/dev/null 2>&1; env' > env.txt\ngrep -qx 'RELAY_ENV=prod' env.txt; ra_cp $? \"exports RELAY_ENV=prod\" \"RELAY_ENV not in the exported environment\"\ngrep -q \"^PATH=$HOME/ops/bin:\" env.txt; ra_cp $? \"puts HOME/ops/bin first on PATH\" \"$(grep ^PATH= env.txt)\"\nset -f; set -- $cron; set +f\n{ [ \"$1\" = \"*/15\" ] || [ \"$1\" = \"0,15,30,45\" ]; } && [ \"$2 $3 $4 $5\" = \"* * * *\" ]; ra_cp $? \"cron line runs sweep.sh every 15 minutes\" \"schedule was: $1 $2 $3 $4 $5\"\nprintf '%s' \"$cron\" | grep -qE '>> *\"?/var/log/sweep\\.log\"? +2>&1|&>> *\"?/var/log/sweep\\.log'; ra_cp $? \"cron line appends stdout and stderr to the log\" \"command was: $cron\"\n","sh12":"# @cp blocks IPs with more than 20 hits | ignores quiet IPs | exits 0 on success | unreadable or missing log exits 1\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\n: > big.log\nfor p in \"10.0.0.66 31\" \"8.8.4.4 25\" \"10.0.0.7 20\" \"1.1.1.1 3\"; do set -- $p; for i in $(seq \"$2\"); do echo \"$1 GET /x $i\" >> big.log; done; done\nra_run big.log\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -q '10\\.0\\.0\\.66' && printf '%s\\n' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -q '8\\.8\\.4\\.4'; ra_cp $? \"blocks IPs with more than 20 hits\" \"$RA_OUT\"\n! printf '%s\\n' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -qE '10\\.0\\.0\\.7\\b|1\\.1\\.1\\.1'; ra_cp $? \"ignores quiet IPs\" \"20 hits isn't more than 20; output: $RA_OUT\"\n[ \"$RA_CODE\" = 0 ]; ra_cp $? \"exits 0 on success\" \"exit $RA_CODE, stderr: $RA_ERR\"\nra_run missing.log; [ \"$RA_CODE\" = 1 ]; ra_cp $? \"unreadable or missing log exits 1\" \"exit $RA_CODE\"\n","sh2":"# @cp counts BLACKOUT lines in any case, minus TEST\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\nprintf '%s\\n' \"BLACKOUT grid 7\" \"blackout harbor\" \"TEST BLACKOUT drill\" \"all clear\" \"Blackout north\" > relay.log\nra_run\nra_eq \"counts BLACKOUT lines in any case, minus TEST\" \"$(echo $RA_OUT)\" \"3\"\n","sh3":"# @cp prints STAMP: HITS failures in TARGET\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\nprintf '%s\\n' \"10:00 FAIL login\" \"10:01 OK\" \"10:02 FAIL token\" \"10:03 FAILOVER started\" > relay.log\nra_run\nra_eq \"prints STAMP: HITS failures in TARGET\" \"$RA_OUT\" \"$(date +%F): 3 failures in relay.log\"\n","sh4":"# @cp no argument prints usage and exits 1 | existing file prints scanning and exits 0 | missing file exits 2\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\necho data > target.log\nra_run; [ \"$RA_CODE\" = 1 ] && printf '%s' \"$RA_OUT$RA_ERR\" | grep -qi usage; ra_cp $? \"no argument prints usage and exits 1\" \"exit $RA_CODE, output: $RA_OUT\"\nra_run target.log; [ \"$RA_CODE\" = 0 ] && printf '%s' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -qi scanning; ra_cp $? \"existing file prints scanning and exits 0\" \"exit $RA_CODE, output: $RA_OUT\"\nra_run nope.log; [ \"$RA_CODE\" = 2 ]; ra_cp $? \"missing file exits 2\" \"exit $RA_CODE\"\n","sh5":"# @cp reports each host up or down | reads every line, including one with no trailing newline\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\ncat > bin/ping <<'P'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nfor a in \"$@\"; do h=\"$a\"; done\necho \"PING $h\"; case \"$h\" in up-*) exit 0 ;; *) exit 1 ;; esac\nP\nchmod +x bin/ping\nprintf 'up-north\\ndown-harbor\\nup-relay\\n' > hosts.txt\nra_run\nra_eq \"reports each host up or down\" \"$RA_OUT\" \"$(printf 'up-north up\\ndown-harbor down\\nup-relay up')\"\nprintf 'up-a\\nup-b' > hosts.txt\nra_run\n[ \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -c ' up$')\" -ge 1 ]; ra_cp $? \"reads every line, including one with no trailing newline\" \"$RA_OUT\"\n","sh6":"# @cp archives src into dest | defaults dest to /tmp | missing src returns 1\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\nmkdir -p intel out; echo secret > intel/a.txt\nra_run intel out\ntar -tzf out/intel.tar.gz 2>/dev/null | grep -q 'a.txt'; ra_cp $? \"archives src into dest\" \"out/intel.tar.gz missing or doesn't contain intel/a.txt (exit $RA_CODE)\"\nD=\"ra_default_$$_$RANDOM\"; mkdir \"$D\"; echo x > \"$D/x\"\nra_run \"$D\"\n[ -f \"/tmp/$D.tar.gz\" ]; ra_cp $? \"defaults dest to /tmp\" \"/tmp/$D.tar.gz not created\"; rm -f \"/tmp/$D.tar.gz\"\nra_run does-not-exist out; [ \"$RA_CODE\" = 1 ]; ra_cp $? \"missing src returns 1\" \"exit $RA_CODE\"\n","sh7":"# @cp prints the top 5 IPs by request count | prints exactly 5 rows | clean.log redacts every token | clean.log keeps the rest of each line\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\n: > access.log\nfor p in \"10.0.0.1 9\" \"10.0.0.2 7\" \"8.8.8.8 12\" \"10.0.0.3 2\" \"1.1.1.1 5\" \"10.0.0.4 4\" \"10.0.0.5 1\"; do set -- $p; for i in $(seq \"$2\"); do echo \"$1 - - GET /api/$i 200\" >> access.log; done; done\nprintf '%s\\n' \"user=neo token=abc123 action=login\" \"token=zz9 path=/ token=qq\" \"no secrets here\" > app.log\nra_run\ntop=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -oE '([0-9]+\\.){3}[0-9]+' | head -n 5 | tr '\\n' ' ')\nra_eq \"prints the top 5 IPs by request count\" \"$top\" \"8.8.8.8 10.0.0.1 10.0.0.2 1.1.1.1 10.0.0.4 \"\nra_eq \"prints exactly 5 rows\" \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -cE '([0-9]+\\.){3}[0-9]+')\" \"5\"\n[ -f clean.log ] && ! grep -qE 'token=(abc123|zz9|qq)' clean.log && [ \"$(grep -o 'token=REDACTED' clean.log | wc -l)\" = 3 ]; ra_cp $? \"clean.log redacts every token\" \"$(cat clean.log 2>/dev/null | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\ngrep -q 'user=neo token=REDACTED action=login' clean.log 2>/dev/null && grep -q 'no secrets here' clean.log; ra_cp $? \"clean.log keeps the rest of each line\" \"$(cat clean.log 2>/dev/null | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\n","sh8":"# @cp sweep.sh is mode 700 | the SSH key is mode 600 | cryptominer received SIGTERM\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\necho 'echo sweep' > sweep.sh; chmod 644 sweep.sh\nmkdir -p \"$HOME/.ssh\"; echo KEY > \"$HOME/.ssh/id_ed25519\"; chmod 644 \"$HOME/.ssh/id_ed25519\"\nprintf '#!/bin/bash\\nwhile :; do sleep 0.1; done\\n' > bin/cryptominer; chmod +x bin/cryptominer\ncryptominer 30 & MINER=$!\nsleep 0.2\npgrep cryptominer >/dev/null 2>&1 || { printf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n[ \"${@: -1}\" = cryptominer ] && echo %s\\n' \"$MINER\" > bin/pgrep; chmod +x bin/pgrep; }\nra_run\nra_eq \"sweep.sh is mode 700\" \"$(stat -c %a sweep.sh)\" \"700\"\nra_eq \"the SSH key is mode 600\" \"$(stat -c %a \"$HOME/.ssh/id_ed25519\")\" \"600\"\nwait \"$MINER\" 2>/dev/null; st=$?\n[ \"$st\" = 143 ]; ra_cp $? \"cryptominer received SIGTERM\" \"process exit status $st (143 means SIGTERM; 0 means it was never killed)\"\n","sh9":"# @cp healthy relay exits 0 | down relay prints relay down to stderr and exits 3 | trap removes the temp dir\n#@@PRELUDE@@\nRA_ROOT=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$RA_ROOT\" || exit 1\nmkdir -p bin home tmp; export PATH=\"$RA_ROOT/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$RA_ROOT/home\" TMPDIR=\"$RA_ROOT/tmp\"\ncat > user.sh <<'__RA_USER__'\n#@@USER@@\n__RA_USER__\nra_run() { bash user.sh \"$@\" > out.txt 2> err.txt; RA_CODE=$?; RA_OUT=$(cat out.txt); RA_ERR=$(cat err.txt); }\ncat > bin/curl <<'C'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nif [ \"${RA_RELAY:-up}\" = up ]; then echo '{\"status\":\"ok\"}'; exit 0; fi\necho \"curl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 503\" >&2; exit 22\nC\nchmod +x bin/curl\nRA_RELAY=up ra_run; [ \"$RA_CODE\" = 0 ]; ra_cp $? \"healthy relay exits 0\" \"exit $RA_CODE, stderr: $RA_ERR\"\nRA_RELAY=down; export RA_RELAY; ra_run; unset RA_RELAY\n[ \"$RA_CODE\" = 3 ] && printf '%s' \"$RA_ERR\" | grep -q 'relay down' && ! printf '%s' \"$RA_OUT\" | grep -q 'relay down'; ra_cp $? \"down relay prints relay down to stderr and exits 3\" \"exit $RA_CODE, stdout: $RA_OUT, stderr: $RA_ERR\"\n[ -z \"$(ls -A \"$TMPDIR\")\" ]; ra_cp $? \"trap removes the temp dir\" \"left behind: $(ls \"$TMPDIR\" | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\n","sw1":"// @cp intro(handle: \"neo\", level: 3) | intro(handle: \"trinity\", level: 12)\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nraEq(\"intro(handle: \\\"neo\\\", level: 3)\", intro(handle: \"neo\", level: 3), \"Agent neo // level 3\")\nraEq(\"intro(handle: \\\"trinity\\\", level: 12)\", intro(handle: \"trinity\", level: 12), \"Agent trinity // level 12\")\n","sw10":"// @cp ping returns a Bool | Ledger records hits | sweep counts reachable hosts\n// @ci-only Needs Swift 5.5+ concurrency (async/await, actors, task groups). Judge0 has Swift 5.2, so this runs on Swift 6 in GitHub Actions.\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nlet raP = await ping(\"north\")\nraCp(raP == true, \"ping returns a Bool\", \"ping(\\\"north\\\") = \\(raP)\")\nlet raL = Ledger()\nawait raL.record(); await raL.record()\nraEq(\"Ledger records hits\", await raL.total(), 2)\nraEq(\"sweep counts reachable hosts\", await sweep([\"a\", \"\", \"c\"]), 2)\n","sw11":"// @cp Your @Test suite | Includes a parameterized test\n// @ci-only Swift Testing (@Test, #expect) needs Swift 6 and `swift test`. Runs in GitHub Actions on macOS.\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\n","sw12":"// @cp ConsoleView builds | body renders\n// @ci-only SwiftUI and @Observable need Apple's SDK (macOS 14+). Runs in GitHub Actions on a macOS runner.\nimport SwiftUI\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nlet raView = ConsoleView()\nraCp(true, \"ConsoleView builds\")\nlet raBody = raView.body\nraCp(String(describing: type(of: raBody)).count > 0, \"body renders\")\n","sw2":"// @cp score 95 | score 90 | score 60 | score 59 | score 30 | score 0 | validPin accepts 6 digits | validPin rejects bad input\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nfor (s, w) in [(95, \"CRITICAL\"), (90, \"CRITICAL\"), (60, \"HIGH\"), (59, \"MEDIUM\"), (30, \"MEDIUM\"), (0, \"LOW\")] {\n    raEq(\"score \\(s)\", threatLevel(s), w)\n}\nraCp(validPin(\"123456\"), \"validPin accepts 6 digits\")\nraCp(!validPin(\"12345\") && !validPin(\"12a456\") && !validPin(\"\"), \"validPin rejects bad input\")\n","sw3":"// @cp finds a known name | falls back to default | unknown with no default\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nraEq(\"finds a known name\", lookup(\"relay\", in: [\"relay\": \"10.0.0.4\", \"default\": \"0.0.0.0\"]), \"10.0.0.4\")\nraEq(\"falls back to default\", lookup(\"ghost\", in: [\"relay\": \"10.0.0.4\", \"default\": \"0.0.0.0\"]), \"0.0.0.0\")\nlet raR = lookup(\"ghost\", in: [\"relay\": \"10.0.0.4\"])\nraCp(!raR.isEmpty && raR != \"10.0.0.4\", \"unknown with no default\", \"got \\(raR)\")\n","sw4":"// @cp tally counts repeats | tally empty | loud filters then maps\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nlet raT = tally([\"10.0.0.9\", \"10.0.0.4\", \"10.0.0.9\"])\nraCp(raT[\"10.0.0.9\"] == 2 && raT[\"10.0.0.4\"] == 1 && raT.count == 2, \"tally counts repeats\", \"\\(raT)\")\nraEq(\"tally empty\", tally([]).count, 0)\nraEq(\"loud filters then maps\", loud([22, 8080, 443, 3000]), [80800, 30000])\n","sw5":"// @cp scan uses the default port | scan with an explicit port | retry stops on success | retry gives up | onAlert stores handlers\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nraCp(scan(host: \"relay\").contains(\"443\"), \"scan uses the default port\", scan(host: \"relay\"))\nraCp(scan(host: \"relay\", port: 22).contains(\"22\"), \"scan with an explicit port\", scan(host: \"relay\", port: 22))\nvar raCalls = 0\nlet raOk = retry(times: 5) { raCalls += 1; return raCalls == 2 }\nraCp(raOk && raCalls == 2, \"retry stops on success\", \"returned \\(raOk) after \\(raCalls) calls\")\nraCalls = 0\nlet raNo = retry(times: 3) { raCalls += 1; return false }\nraCp(!raNo && raCalls == 3, \"retry gives up\", \"returned \\(raNo) after \\(raCalls) calls\")\nlet raBefore = handlers.count\nvar raFired = false\nonAlert { raFired = true }\nhandlers.last?()\nraCp(handlers.count == raBefore + 1 && raFired, \"onAlert stores handlers\", \"handlers.count \\(handlers.count)\")\n","sw6":"// @cp boost mutates the struct | isHot is computed | structs copy by value | Session keeps its id\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nvar raN = Node(name: \"north\", strength: 50)\nraN.boost(10)\nraEq(\"boost mutates the struct\", raN.strength, 60)\nvar raHot = Node(name: \"core\", strength: 100)\nvar raCold = Node(name: \"cold\", strength: 0)\nraCp(raHot.isHot && !raCold.isHot, \"isHot is computed\")\nvar raCopy = raN\nraCopy.boost(5)\nraCp(raN.strength == 60 && raCopy.strength == 65, \"structs copy by value\")\nraEq(\"Session keeps its id\", Session(id: \"s-1\").id, \"s-1\")\n","sw7":"// @cp parses a valid port | empty string throws empty | garbage throws badPort\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nraEq(\"parses a valid port\", (try? parsePort(\"443\")) ?? -1, 443)\ndo { _ = try parsePort(\"\"); raCp(false, \"empty string throws empty\", \"no error thrown\") }\ncatch ScanError.empty { raCp(true, \"empty string throws empty\") }\ncatch { raCp(false, \"empty string throws empty\", \"threw \\(error)\") }\ndo { _ = try parsePort(\"http\"); raCp(false, \"garbage throws badPort\", \"no error thrown\") }\ncatch ScanError.badPort(_) { raCp(true, \"garbage throws badPort\") }\ncatch { raCp(false, \"garbage throws badPort\", \"threw \\(error)\") }\n","sw8":"// @cp login mentions the user | breach mentions severity | high severity uses the where case | logout | Faction is CaseIterable with raw values\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nlet raA = describe(.login(user: \"neo\"))\nraCp(raA.contains(\"neo\"), \"login mentions the user\", raA)\nlet raB = describe(.breach(severity: 3))\nraCp(raB.contains(\"3\"), \"breach mentions severity\", raB)\nlet raC = describe(.breach(severity: 10))\nlet raD = describe(.breach(severity: 1))\nraCp(raC.filter { !$0.isNumber } != raD.filter { !$0.isNumber }, \"high severity uses the where case\", \"severity 10: \\(raC) / severity 1: \\(raD)\")\nraCp(!describe(.logout).isEmpty, \"logout\")\nraCp(Faction.allCases.count >= 2 && !Faction.allCases[0].rawValue.isEmpty, \"Faction is CaseIterable with raw values\")\n","sw9":"// @cp Keyword detects | count(in:) default implementation | strongest of ints | strongest of empty\n//@@USER@@\n//@@PRELUDE@@\nlet raK = Keyword(word: \"jndi\")\nraCp(raK.detect(\"${jndi:x}\") && !raK.detect(\"hello\"), \"Keyword detects\")\nraEq(\"count(in:) default implementation\", raK.count(in: [\"jndi a\", \"b\", \"c jndi\"]), 2)\nraEq(\"strongest of ints\", strongest([3, 9, 2]), 9)\nraCp(strongest([Int]()) == nil, \"strongest of empty\")\n"}); })(typeof window !== "undefined" ? window : globalThis);

